WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.817
This example updates the city value through a simple view.

00:00:03.817 --> 00:00:08.132
The returning clause immediately shows the row that would be changed.

00:00:08.132 --> 00:00:14.227
Then the transaction is rolled back, so the teaching database returns to its original state.

00:00:14.227 --> 00:00:16.842
This is a useful testing pattern.

00:00:16.842 --> 00:00:24.162
Make the change inside a transaction, inspect what happened, and keep or undo the change only after you understand the

00:00:24.162 --> 00:00:25.076
result.
